{
  "id": "unconscious-transfer",
  "term": "unconscious transfer",
  "definition": "Unconscious transfer is the automatic carrying over of feelings and attitudes from important people in early life onto other people in the present, including a psychotherapist. In counselling or psychotherapy, this means old emotional patterns are directed toward the therapist without the person being aware of it.",
